From cf2fd74d3a09a6a0249aaf102177237afb8e1842 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:16:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Preconditioner built on the assembled tangent operator
 (AssembledOperator)

With the tangent operator applied without assembly (MatrixFree), the
preconditioner may be built on the tangent operator assembled by
kernels: new AssembledOperator preconditioner of the linear solvers,
wrapping another preconditioner (for instance HypreBoomerAMG), set up on
the assembled operator every UpdatePeriod calls to SetOperator (one per
Newton iteration), and kept between them. The Krylov solver uses the
action of the kernels. An operator which can't give an assembled
version, as the assembled operator of the prediction, is given directly
to the wrapped preconditioner.

The operator applied without assembly gives its assembled version
through the AssembledOperatorProvider interface, implemented by
ConstrainedMatrixFreeTangentOperator (mfem::ConstrainedOperator), the
assembly by kernels of the tangent operator on the true degrees of
freedom being now a method of NonLinearEvolutionProblemImplementation
(assembleTangentOperatorByKernels), shared with the Kernels value of
TangentOperatorComputation.

BatchIntegrationTest: matrix free computations with this preconditioner
(BoomerAMG in parallel, Jacobi in sequential), compared to the
integration point by point.
